From: Fukui Daichi <a.dog.will.talk@akane.waseda.jp>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: Add missing Makefile dependencies

alm_tools.F90 uses the healpix_sharp_f90 module, but nothing ensured
that healpix_sharp_f90.o (and therefore healpix_sharp_f90.mod) was built
before alm_tools.o. The build thus only succeeded thanks to the order of
prerequisites in $(obj), and failed with make --shuffle=reverse or with
some parallel builds:

  Fatal Error: Cannot open module file 'healpix_sharp_f90.mod' for reading

Also make the creation of the build directory an order-only prerequisite
of every object instead of relying on the order of prerequisites of
'all'.

Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1105399
Forwarded: no
---
 src/f90/mod/Makefile | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/f90/mod/Makefile b/src/f90/mod/Makefile
--- a/src/f90/mod/Makefile
+++ b/src/f90/mod/Makefile
@@ -69,6 +69,13 @@ $(obj5:%=$(OD)/%): $(obj4:%=$(OD)/%)
 $(obj6:%=$(OD)/%): $(obj5:%=$(OD)/%)
 $(obj7:%=$(OD)/%): $(obj6:%=$(OD)/%)
 
+# alm_tools uses the healpix_sharp_f90 module, which is not part of the
+# chain above
+$(OD)/alm_tools.o: $(OD)/healpix_sharp_f90.o
+
+# the build directory must exist before any object is written into it
+$(OBJ): | $(OD)_mkdir
+
 $(OD)/%.o: $(SD)/%.c
 	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -c $< -o $@
 
